# Fuzzing. The build directory and the evolving corpora are generated: libFuzzer
# rewrites the corpus on every run, so committing it would mean thousands of
# churning binary files for no reproducibility gain — the seeds in
# `fuzz/tests/corpus.rs` and `testdata/` are what a run starts from.
# `fuzz/artifacts/` is deliberately NOT ignored: a crash reproducer is committed
# so `fuzz/tests/corpus.rs` replays it on every commit thereafter.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/

# Container / distribution archives
sandesh.tar
sandesh.tar.gz
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# Runtime workspace state. `WorkspaceManager::load_or_init` creates the
# directory and seeds the registry on first run, so neither is a build input
# and a checkout without them is correct. They land in the repo root only
# because the dev data_dir resolves to the working directory.
# Tracking them means every developer's local message blobs and `active_id`
# flips show up as diffs and conflict on merge.
/workspaces/
/workspaces.json

# ---- Open-source release ----
# Generated by scripts/third_party_notices.py at release time; the source of
# truth is Cargo.lock and web/package-lock.json.
/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt
# Exported copies of docs/MASTER_USER_MANUAL.md, never versioned: 11 MB of binaries that churn
# on every edit. The Markdown manual is the maintained one.
docs/MASTER_USER_MANUAL.docx
docs/MASTER_USER_MANUAL.pdf
docs/temp_raw.docx

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
